1.	Define project objectives – Clearly identify the goals of the project.
	2.	Identify project tasks – Break the project into smaller activities.
	3.	Create a schedule – Decide the timeline and deadlines for each task.
	4.	Assign responsibilities – Decide who will handle each task.
	5.	Estimate resources – Identify required software, hardware, tools, and people.
	6.	Estimate cost – Calculate the expected project expenses.
	7.	Identify risks – Find possible problems and prepare solutions.
	8.	Set milestones – Define important stages and completion points.
	9.	Prepare the project plan – Document the complete schedule, resources, responsibilities, and risks.
